                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling or full of slivers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9aef075-06c5-475c-b907-19229a5734b9",
                                "sense_id": "519a2f51-0cc5-3baa-9670-f3aa59250a75",
                                "text": "Mimi, unfortunately, was not dressed to slide on the slivery surface of new-sawed pine. […] [H]er costume of pink silk and chiffon, not overly voluminous in the first place, mostly was impaled on slivers and left in her wake; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e378c93a-ceb6-4935-8d42-f1394b530cd0",
                                "sense_id": "519a2f51-0cc5-3baa-9670-f3aa59250a75",
                                "text": "As a final touch she made some slivery little brown-and-white-bread sandwiches to go with the Newburg, just for style."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfde5218-722e-4d8a-9137-ed37474c9296",
                                "sense_id": "519a2f51-0cc5-3baa-9670-f3aa59250a75",
                                "text": "A common defect in copper wire is that of slivers. These may be caused by improperly cast wire bars and/or by improper hot rolling. Horizontally cast wire bars having cold shuts, rough edges and bad sets, will make slivery rod and wire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
